# Vercel builds the frontend only; the API is a container on Render.
#
# This exists for a second reason beyond upload size: the CLI scans the upload
# for frameworks, finds serve.py, detects a FastAPI service, and then refuses a
# root-level buildCommand as ambiguous. Keeping Python out of the upload keeps
# the detection on Vite, which is the only thing here Vercel actually builds.
#
# contract/openapi.json is deliberately NOT ignored: `npm run build` regenerates
# web/src/api/schema.d.ts from it, which is why the build must run from the repo
# root rather than from web/.
*.py
contract/stub_server.py
artifacts/
sundai_cgm/
build/
.venv/
.github/
Dockerfile
requirements*.txt
uv.lock
